Traccar
-------

Traccar (https://github.com/traccar/traccar)
Copyright Anton Tananaev and Traccar contributors
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

No Traccar source code is included. Traccar was used in two ways:

1. Test data. Device packets published in Traccar's protocol decoder tests
   (src/test/java/org/traccar/protocol) are used, as protocol facts, as
   test vectors in these files:
   - gt06/gt06_test.go: GT06/Concox frames, also quoted in the protocol
     documents.
   - gt06/lbs_test.go: GT06/Concox cell (LBS) and WiFi frames from the GT06
     tests; gt06/lbs.go's frame layouts were checked against them.
   - jt808/decode_test.go: the JT/T 808 frames of the vRegister2013 to
     vRegister2019 block (2013 and 2019 registration, authentication,
     location, locate answer, batch and blind-area uploads, a 0x6006 text
     answer), from Jt808ProtocolDecoderTest.
   - h02/decode_test.go: H02 binary records bDoc, bText and b45.
   - ruptela/ruptela_test.go: Ruptela packets devRecords, devIdent,
     devGetio and devExt.
   - ais140/ais140_test.go: AIS-140 packets of several manufacturers
     (fieldVectors).
   - osmand/decode_test.go: OsmAnd sample requests and older Traccar
     Client JSON bodies (OsmAndProtocolDecoderTest).

2. Reference reading for behaviour, without taking code: the H02 decoder
   and encoder, the JT808 decoder and encoder ("huabao"), the OsmAnd
   decoder, and the Position and Device models whose JSON field names a
   Traccar server's position forwarding carries (osmand/json.go reads
   them). PROVENANCE.md says what was taken from each.

Traccar's web site also hosts manufacturers' protocol documents
(traccar.org/protocol/...); those are the manufacturers' documents, cited
in PROVENANCE.md, not Traccar's work.

